rite subscripts as separate lines or repeated words.\n   BAD:  "A\\nbolt\\nA \\nbolt"   GOOD:  "A_bolt"\n6. Write math as readable text: "F_total = P × A" not as LaTeX expressions.\n7. Use ## headings. Every heading MUST have a blank line before it.\n8. Keep each sentence SHORT. No run-on paragraphs.\n\nIMPORTANT rules for \'validation_result\':\n- Set \'valid\' to true if the calculation executed correctly, false if there were errors.\n- The \'warnings\' list must NEVER be empty. Always include at least one warning.\n\nCRITICAL NUMBER FORMATTING RULES:\n1. Do NOT round any float values (e.g. return 8482.5 instead of 8483).\n2. Do NOT use scientific notation (e.g. return 25727.5 instead of 2.57e4 or 25700).\n3. Always return exact raw floating-point calculations in the calculation_result dictionary.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Calculate the force for a mass of 18.11 kg accelerating at 2.78 m/s^2.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "[Called tools]: calculate_force({'acceleration': 2.78, 'mass': 18.11})"}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "[Tool result for 'calculate_force']:\n50.3458"}], 'model': 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 'n': 1, 'reasoning_effort': None, 'reasoning_format': None, 'service_tier': 'on_demand', 'stop': None, 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0.7}}
